{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_124","type":"agent_message","text":"Implemented a working Rust translation for the `sha2` backend in `Cargo.toml` and `src/`, including the shared core, RNG, exported signing API, and `driver`. The translated driver now produces the same digest as the C driver for:\n- `sha2 robust 128s`: `6C418BBDEF13E75CCA09A319F4ADFF937067AE432B91C62CCD68C7EC81847264`\n- `sha2 simple 128s`: `3D3F14B889F47078C4524F3F6ADF6EB69C268AFD878379803CF02E2728EB4505`\n\nI also compile-checked the remaining SHA2 parameter sets for both `robust` and `simple`:\n`128f`, `192s`, `192f`, `256s`, `256f`.\n\nThis is not yet a complete solution to your full request. The `shake`, `blake`, and `haraka` backends are still unimplemented, so the project does not yet satisfy “all C source files / all feature combinations”. One practical note: I added `rlib` alongside `cdylib` in `[lib].crate-type` so the local `driver` binary can link against the library crate during Cargo builds."}}
